WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:06.210
In Season 6 of Game of Thrones, Arya says
she wants to go “west of Westeros”, to

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.800
see “The edge of the world”.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.230
West of Westeros is “where all the maps
stop” . No one knows what’s beyond the

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.860
Sunset Sea.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.060
But some have tried to find out.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.939
One of Arya’s ancestors, Brandon the Shipwright,
sailed west ’cross the Sunset Sea – and

00:00:21.939 --> 00:00:28.829
he “was never seen again”, his tomb in
Winterfell is empty . Some crazy ironborn

00:00:28.829 --> 00:00:33.550
on the island of Lonely Light believe there’s
a “paradise” in the west, “a land without

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:39.070
winter or want” – but all they’ve ever
found is “boundless grey” sea . One of

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:44.420
Daenerys’ ancestors, Queen Rhaenys Targaryen,
planned to fly her dragon ’cross the Sea

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:48.150
– but she and her dragon died before she
could try.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:53.880
So the Sunset Sea is a mystery, but there’s
one person who went further west than anyone

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:54.880
else.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:01:00.370
Two hundred and fifty years ago, Elissa Farman
was the daughter of the lord of Fair Isle

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:06.430
– an island off the westerlands, “by the
Sunset Sea” . Elissa was kind of like Arya

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:09.220
– a rebellious wild-spirited girl.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:14.940
She was an archer, and a singer, loved horses
and dogs, “but her great love was sailing”.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.440
She spent most of her childhood on ships.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:23.400
As a teenager, she sailed her own boat, voyaging
north to Bear Island, and south to the Arbor.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:28.290
But her dream was to sail west, and find strange
lands beyond the Sunset Sea .

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:35.990
Elissa’s brother Androw married Rhaena Targaryen
– a widowed queen of two different kings.

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:41.409
It was weird that a queen would marry into
a “minor” family like the Farmans , and

00:01:41.409 --> 00:01:43.860
Androw was a pretty unimpressive husband.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:48.310
Rhaena didn’t seem that into him – she
was closer with Elissa.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:54.891
It’s hinted that Rhaena was gay , and that
she and Elissa were in love . So for a year,

00:01:54.891 --> 00:01:57.220
Rhaena and Elissa and friends lived on Fair
Isle.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:02.420
They were “the center of court life” , and
went on joyrides on Rhaena’s dragon Dreamfyre

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:07.670
. But the Lord of Fair Isle got sick of Rhaena
dominating his island, and of her dragon eating

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:10.929
his sheep – so he asked her to leave.

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:16.219
He wanted Elissa to stay and get married . But
like Arya, Elissa didn’t want to marry some

00:02:16.219 --> 00:02:17.219
lord.

00:02:17.219 --> 00:02:19.409
So she left home with Rhaena.

00:02:19.409 --> 00:02:24.359
For a month, they mooched off the Lannisters
at Casterly Rock, and enjoyed “the hospitality

00:02:24.359 --> 00:02:30.069
of the wealthiest house” in Westeros . But
it turned out, shockingly, that the Lannisters

00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:32.359
were scheming , so Rhaena and co.

00:02:32.359 --> 00:02:37.559
left the Rock, and toured the westerlands
and riverlands for while . As the young daughter

00:02:37.559 --> 00:02:43.390
of a minor noble family, Elissa got to travel
across Westeros with her love, the dragon

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:44.769
queen.

00:02:44.769 --> 00:02:50.379
But eventually, Rhaena settled on Dragonstone,
the Targaryen island . And Elissa wasn’t

00:02:50.379 --> 00:02:55.139
happy there – she wanted to build a ship,
and return to “her wide western seas”

00:02:55.139 --> 00:03:00.529
. Rhaena refused, and their relationship broke
down . So Elissa left Dragonstone, and her

00:03:00.529 --> 00:03:04.319
the way out, she stole three of Rhaena’s
dragon eggs.

00:03:04.319 --> 00:03:09.730
Elissa went to Pentos, then Braavos, and sold
the eggs to the Sealord of Braavos.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:15.329
She used the money to build the ship of her
dreams – the Sun Chaser , designed for deep

00:03:15.329 --> 00:03:21.099
waters and long voyages . Elissa planned to
sail west.

00:03:21.099 --> 00:03:23.989
The Targaryens, meanwhile, lost their shit.

00:03:23.989 --> 00:03:28.811
The theft of their eggs meant that someone
outside their family could get dragons, which

00:03:28.811 --> 00:03:34.730
is like someone outside your country getting
nukes . They hope that without the heat of

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:39.839
Dragonstone, the eggs will “turn to stone”
– that way “some spicemonger in Pentos”

00:03:39.839 --> 00:03:45.909
will only have “three very costly stones”
. Hundreds of years later, in Book 1 of Game

00:03:45.909 --> 00:03:52.769
of Thrones, Illyrio Mopatis, a “cheesemonger”
in Pentos , gives Daenerys three dragon eggs,

00:03:52.769 --> 00:03:57.780
which he says have “turned … to stone”
. Three stone eggs from a “monger” in

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:58.780
Pentos.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:04.299
The language is the same, hinting that Dany’s
eggs are the same eggs that Elissa stole hundreds

00:04:04.299 --> 00:04:05.569
of years ago.

00:04:05.569 --> 00:04:10.680
Daenerys’ whole story might not’ve happened
without Elissa Farman.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:16.090
But author George Martin does say this is
meant to be ambiguous, not certain .

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:19.280
But Elissa built her ship, the Sun Chaser.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:24.670
And from Braavos, she sailed down the narrow
sea, dodging pirates, went around Dorne, and

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:28.720
came to Oldtown , the city of the Citadel
and the Hightower.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:32.810
Elissa knew the Targaryens were hunting her,
looking for their eggs – but she needed

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:37.920
a crew, people who believed in her mission
to find new lands in the west.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:43.300
Which was difficult, because many people believed
that the world just ends in the west, with

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:48.450
“walls of fire and boiling seas”, or “black
fogs that [go] on forever”.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:53.360
But the maesters, and author George Martin,
say that the world of Game of Thrones “is

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:59.030
round” like ours . So the west must eventually
connect to the far east, to the lands of Yi

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:04.510
Ti and Asshai . A western trade route to these
places would be worth a fortune in “silks

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:05.570
and spices”.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:09.280
But Elissa’s dream was bigger than money.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:14.770
She believed that the world was “far larger
and far stranger than the maesters imagine”

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:20.250
. She envisioned new undiscovered lands in-between
Westeros and Essos – with “sundering rivers”

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:26.390
and “plains”, “green islands”, “strange
beasts”, and “golden cities” beneath

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:31.950
“strange stars” . Westeros is kinda like
Britain , Essos is like Europe and Asia, and

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:37.660
Sothoryos like Africa – so maybe there’s
a continent like America.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:40.380
Elissa hoped to find it.

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:45.380
As she looked for a crew, Eustace and Norman
Hightower came to question her – but Elissa

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:49.460
convinced them to join her mission, adding
their ships to hers.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:54.700
She gathered a crew , and just as the Targaryens
were closing in, Elissa left Oldtown with

00:05:54.700 --> 00:06:00.460
three ships and sailed west . Three years
later, one ship returned.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:07.110
Eustace and his ship came ragged and exhausted
back to Oldtown, and Eustace told the story

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:08.920
of Elissa’s voyage.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:14.110
He said that at first, it was “smooth sailing”
. But a month in, they were hit by storms.

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:19.110
Norman’s ship was struck by lightning, and
sank – some sailors said they saw a kraken

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:24.570
. But Elissa and Eustace’s ships survived,
and they found land – “three small islands”,

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.690
“farther to the west” than any known land.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:33.860
Elissa named the islands Aegon, Visenya and
Rhaenys – so Rhaenys Targaryen, who died

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:39.230
before she got to fly west, had an island
named for her in the far Sunset Sea.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:45.100
Elissa explored her new islands, and found
new spices, pink fruits , and huge grey lizards

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:50.680
with venomous bites . Elissa wanted to sail
further west, to discover more new land.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:54.500
But Eustace and his crew were scared, and
turned back home.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:59.740
Eustace spent a year stuck on Sothoryos and
his crew almost all died, but some Summer

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:02.300
Islanders helped them back to Oldtown.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:05.870
Go watch our video about Sothoryos and the
east.

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:09.880
As for Elissa – she “vanished” to the
west, “still searching for … lands beyond

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:11.530
the Sunset Sea”.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.800
She “was never seen again”.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.069
“Except…”

00:07:15.069 --> 00:07:21.770
Decades later, a famous mariner called Corlys
Velaryon visited Asshai in the far far east.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:26.480
And there, “he glimpsed an old and … weathered
ship that” he said “could only have been

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:29.300
Sun Chaser” , Elissa’s ship.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:33.550
So maybe Elissa made it all the way across
the world.

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:39.080
She coulda seen new lands, and crossed the
Americas, before arriving at Asshai from the

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.120
east.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:42.570
And one theory goes further.

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:47.760
In Book 2, Daenerys meets Quaithe, a shadowbinder
from Asshai.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:50.730
And Quaithe says “To go north, you must
journey south.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:56.669
To reach the west, you must go east” – just
like Elissa goes west to reach the east.

00:07:56.669 --> 00:08:00.500
So some fans speculate that Quaithe is Elissa.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:05.840
That she learned magic in Asshai, and lengthened
her life – just like Melisandre of Asshai

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:12.230
lengthens her life . Maybe Quaithe-lissa helps
Daenerys because she reminds her of Rhaena,

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:15.480
the dragon queen Elissa once loved.

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:20.810
The reason why Quaithe comes to Dany in the
first place is to see her dragons – the

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:27.010
dragons that hatched from the eggs that Elissa
stole . So this is just speculation, but it’s

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:32.769
possible that Elissa Farman still lives as
a two-hundred and fifty year old magician

00:08:32.769 --> 00:08:35.669
with a cool mask and a love for geography.

00:08:35.669 --> 00:08:41.930
It’s also possible that Elissa just died
at sea, or on some unknown land.

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:47.740
What we do know is that Elissa rebelled against
her family, and loved a dragon queen.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:54.110
She travelled across Westeros and beyond,
following a dream to see sights yet unseen.

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:57.889
And maybe rebellious Arya could do the same.

00:08:57.889 --> 00:09:01.490
Like Elissa, she could reject the life that
others chose for her.

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:04.980
She could escape the violence and horror that
she’s suffered.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:10.019
Like Elissa, Arya could sail west, chasing
the sun.

00:09:10.019 --> 00:09:14.579
Of course, circumnavigating the globe takes
more than an adventurous spirit.

00:09:14.579 --> 00:09:20.009
Naval navigation without modern technology
involves a lot of math – geometry, trigonometry,

00:09:20.009 --> 00:09:21.009
astronomy.

00:09:21.009 --> 00:09:24.880
But people have done it for thousands of years.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:29.809
The ancient Greeks accurately calculated the
size of the earth . Columbus and Magellan

00:09:29.809 --> 00:09:32.139
knew the earth was round.

00:09:32.139 --> 00:09:37.079
Maybe Elissa Farman did too.

00:09:37.079 --> 00:09:40.519
Maybe Elissa Farman used Brilliant.

00:09:40.519 --> 00:09:45.009
Brilliant is a learning site with interactive
challenges teaching maths and science.

00:09:45.009 --> 00:09:49.420
It’s better than a lecture or video, cause
it has you actually solving problems yourself

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:53.500
at your own pace, with guides and solutions
to help you through.

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:58.320
It starts with basic stuff, then more advanced,
then… whatever this is

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:00.900
With Brilliant, you can find out.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:05.600
It's surprisingly easy and fun to learn all
the concepts you missed at school - and to

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.550
become a little smarter each day.

